WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.040
The industrial example
distinguishes three gates:

00:00:03.093 --> 00:00:07.000
building, passing reliably
and adding coverage.

00:00:07.130 --> 00:00:10.800
The share of qualifying target test
classes decreases as the requirement

00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:15.600
becomes stronger. These percentages
describe test classes, not individual

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:20.160
generated tests. A successful build
is therefore an intermediate result.

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:23.440
For a local pilot, preserve
this distinction and add

00:00:23.543 --> 00:00:27.120
checks that the assertions
detect important faults.

00:00:27.289 --> 00:00:31.520
Coverage alone does not establish
correct business behavior.
